# Copy to .env and fill in. .env is gitignored (`.env*` in .gitignore) and this
# repository is PUBLIC — a token committed here is a token to revoke.
#
# NPM_TOKEN publishes @bershadsky/metaframework. It must be a **Classic ->
# Automation** token from npmjs.com -> Access Tokens.
#
# Not a Publish token, and not the credential `npm login` wrote to ~/.npmrc:
# this account requires 2FA for writes, the second factor is a security key,
# and npm can only run that ceremony with a TTY (lib/utils/open-url.js returns
# early when stdin is not a TTY). Automation tokens carry the 2FA bypass, which
# is what makes a headless `npm run release` — or a CI release — possible at
# all.
#
# Referenced by framework/portal/.npmrc as ${NPM_TOKEN}; loaded by
# scripts/release.sh.
NPM_TOKEN=
